# Rust build output
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# npm binary-distribution shim (spec 006): generated platform packages (and the
# prebuilt binaries they carry) are assembled from release artifacts at publish
# time, never committed; ditto local install artifacts and the publish-time
# LICENSE copy.
/npm/dist/
/npm/package-lock.json
/npm/LICENSE
node_modules/

# Python binary-distribution shim (spec 007): wheels/sdist are assembled from
# release artifacts at publish time, never committed; ditto the publish-time
# LICENSE copy and local build/test residue.
/py/dist/
/py/LICENSE
/py/src/spec_spine.egg-info/
__pycache__/

# The managed layout (spec 092 3.7, 3.9). `.statecraft/` as a whole is NOT
# ignored and must not be: `.statecraft/derived/` (compiler/indexer output) is
# committed, so the coupling gate and the content-hash staleness check can
# compare the committed registry and index against current inputs. Determinism
# makes this sane. Only two things under it are excluded, and each for its own
# stated reason.
#
# build-meta.json carries a wall-clock `builtAt` (the sole non-deterministic
# artifact), so it would churn on every compile.
.statecraft/derived/**/build-meta.json
# The ledger-seal attestation (spec 021) is an on-demand artifact (and the seal
# carries a wall-clock `signedAt`); it is not part of the committed dogfood set.
.statecraft/derived/attestation/
# `[layout] state_dir` (spec 036): a tool's own working files, ungoverned and
# outside every content hash.
.statecraft/state/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
.env*
# Local secrets (e.g. CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN): never commit
.env

.idea/

# Agent tooling (.claude/) is committed: agents/, rules/, skills/ are the
# curated cross-agent setup CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md reference. But per-agent
# learned memory is local, session-generated state (like the user's own memory
# dir, which lives outside the repo), so it is not version-controlled.
.claude/agent-memory/

# Retain the pre-migration installer directory for existing local worktrees.
.tooling/

# >>> statecraft managed ignores >>>
# Managed by Statecraft. Entries above and below this block are yours and are
# never reordered, rewritten or removed. Delete the whole block to opt out.
# spec-spine: transient metadata and runtime state
#
# spec-spine writes wall-clock metadata here. It is the one
# non-deterministic artifact and is excluded from every determinism and
# golden check, so it must never be committed.

# The declared state root (spec 036): a tool's own working files,
# ungoverned and outside every content hash.

# NOT ignored, deliberately: .statecraft/derived/spec-registry/ and
# .statecraft/derived/codebase-index/ are the committed shard trees.
#
# Committing them is what makes `compile --check` and `index check` a
# freshness gate on a pull request: CI compares the corpus against what
# the branch committed. Not committing them means regenerating in CI
# before every gate step instead. Both are legitimate; the scaffold
# takes neither, because opting you out of the gate silently would be a
# decision made on your behalf. To choose the second, add:
#
#   .statecraft/derived/
# The repository-local spec-spine the setup profile installs.
.bin/
# <<< statecraft managed ignores <<<
